speechtext:
The last sitting of this committee will take place on Friday next. We are going to close up then, absolutely.
And so to suit the conveniences of the Senate committee counsel for the respondent was refused the opportunity of bringing the wintesses which he said he could bring. As we were told by the member for Brant, the charges which were originally made in the petition were not followed up at the trial, but at that time other charges were sub-stitued, and when it was attempted to refute those other charges counsel could not obtain a sufficiently long adjournment. The Senate committee had to get on with its work, it was going to close up, and whether it involved injustice or not did not seem to make very much difference, so no adjournment was granted. If we are in any sense a court of review I say we cannot do other than ask that this bill be not now read a third time;
I am glad to support the amendment.
